STATEMENT: >>>
A maintained projection for a reader: it presents parts of the canon, start to finish, and depends on their wording.

Also: the representation family ([LINK: DEC-NODE-FAMILIES]). It Cites what it presents, may fingerprint each citation so the edge goes dirty when a cited node changes, and nothing in the grid may depend on one. On the sheet's day the grammar had no such type and the whiteboard was a narrative filed as a mechanism; since 2026-08-30 the grammar spells it with WIDGET and TAGS, this page is a tree of them, and the whiteboard was retyped in place under [LINK: DEC-UID-OUTLIVES-TYPE] -- the first retype between two live prefixes. How a tree of narratives becomes a page is [LINK: DEC-NARRATIVE-IS-THE-VIEW-NODE], in the whiteboard-view plan.

State: DEPTH -- sketch for a draft, interface-settled once the operator has read it and let it stand.
